# ==== Purpose ====
#
# This script exercises the multi-threaded applier (MTA) error-shutdown
# cleanup path that releases a Format_description notification which was
# queued for a worker but never consumed.
#
# ==== Background ====
#
# When the Coordinator sees a new Format_description event it queues a
# reference to it in the group slot of the Global Assigned Queue (GAQ),
# via Slave_job_group::new_fd_event, taking a reference on the shared,
# reference-counted Format_description_log_event. A worker normally
# consumes that reference (and clears the slot) when it starts applying
# the group. If the applier stops with an error before the worker
# consumes the notification, the reference is left in the GAQ and must be
# released when the GAQ is torn down. Otherwise the
# Format_description_log_event leaks.
#
# ==== Requirements ====
#
# R1. When the MTA stops with an error while a Format_description
#     notification is still queued and unconsumed in the GAQ,
#     Slave_committed_queue::free_dynamic_items() releases the pending
#     reference at GAQ teardown, so the Format_description_log_event does
#     not leak.
#
# R2. The applier resumes normally once the failure is no longer injected.
#
# ==== Implementation ====
#
# The queued-but-unconsumed window is microseconds wide in a real run and
# is only reached on a Format_description version change, so it cannot be
# hit deterministically from SQL. The debug point
# 'mta_pending_fd_event_on_stop' makes it deterministic: when a worker is
# about to consume the (possibly absent) FD notification for a group, it
# instead installs a queued reference on the shared FD event -- exactly as
# the Coordinator would -- and then errors out before consuming it,
# leaving the reference dangling in the GAQ.
#
# 1. Set up the replica to apply transactions in parallel.
# 2. With the debug point active, run a transaction on the source. The
#    worker errors out with ER_REPLICA_FATAL_ERROR while a queued FD
#    reference is left in the GAQ, and the MTA stops.
# 3. Removing the debug point, restart the applier and check that the
#    transaction is applied.
# 4. Clean up.
#
# Without the fix the pending reference is never released, so the shared
# Format_description_log_event's usage counter never falls to zero and the
# event leaks. In any build with assertions enabled -- including the ASAN
# debug builds this is normally run under -- the dangling reference is caught
# first, as an assertion in Relay_log_info::set_rli_description_event():
#
#   assert(!rli_description_event || is_parallel_exec());
#
# handle_slave_sql() forgets the relay log's format with
# set_rli_description_event(nullptr) only after slave_stop_workers() has torn
# the worker pool down. The GAQ was destroyed there without releasing the
# pending reference, so the counter does not reach zero and the delete is
# skipped. Reaching that branch is legitimate only while MTS is still
# running, and replica_parallel_workers has just been reset to 0, so
# is_parallel_exec() is false and the invariant fails.
#
# The assertion is the only symptom this script can produce: it requires a
# debug server (have_debug.inc), and under NDEBUG the DBUG_EXECUTE_IF holding
# the injection is compiled out, so the leak never happens here in the first
# place. A LeakSanitizer report for the same leak needs an NDEBUG+ASAN build
# hitting the queued-but-unconsumed window for real, without this debug point.
#
# This script makes sure the cleanup path is exercised and that the
# applier behaves as expected around the stop.
#
# ==== References ====
#
# Bug#39319907 Reject oversized packed row values earlier [post fix]
#

--source include/have_debug.inc
--source include/have_binlog_format_row.inc
--source include/not_group_replication_plugin.inc
--source include/master-slave.inc

--echo
--echo # 1. Set up the replica to apply transactions in parallel.

--source include/rpl_connection_slave.inc
CALL mtr.add_suppression("Injected pending Format_description notification at MTA stop");
CALL mtr.add_suppression("The replica coordinator and worker threads are stopped");

SET @saved_parallel_workers= @@GLOBAL.replica_parallel_workers;

--source include/stop_slave.inc
--disable_warnings
SET @@GLOBAL.replica_parallel_workers= 4;
--enable_warnings
--source include/start_slave.inc

--source include/rpl_connection_master.inc
CREATE TABLE t1 (a INT PRIMARY KEY) ENGINE=InnoDB;
--source include/sync_slave_sql_with_master.inc

--echo
--echo # 2. Stop the MTA with a Format_description notification still queued.

--source include/rpl_connection_slave.inc
--source include/stop_slave_sql.inc
--let $debug_point= mta_pending_fd_event_on_stop
--source include/add_debug_point.inc

--source include/rpl_connection_master.inc
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES (1);

--source include/rpl_connection_slave.inc
--disable_warnings
START REPLICA SQL_THREAD;
--enable_warnings
--let $slave_sql_errno= convert_error(ER_REPLICA_FATAL_ERROR)
--source include/wait_for_slave_sql_error.inc

--echo
--echo # 3. The applier resumes once the failure is no longer injected.

--let $debug_point= mta_pending_fd_event_on_stop
--source include/remove_debug_point.inc
--source include/start_slave_sql.inc

--source include/rpl_connection_master.inc
--source include/sync_slave_sql_with_master.inc

--source include/rpl_connection_slave.inc
--let $assert_text= the transaction is applied after resuming the applier
--let $assert_cond= COUNT(*) = 1 FROM t1 WHERE a = 1
--source include/assert.inc

--echo
--echo # 4. Clean up.

--source include/rpl_connection_slave.inc
--source include/stop_slave.inc
--disable_warnings
SET @@GLOBAL.replica_parallel_workers= @saved_parallel_workers;
--enable_warnings
--source include/start_slave.inc

--source include/rpl_connection_master.inc
DROP TABLE t1;
--source include/sync_slave_sql_with_master.inc

--source include/rpl_end.inc
